## Booking workflow

1. User selects a resource.
2. User selects the activity.
3. User selects a date and time.
4. User enters the required purpose and relevant activity details.
5. The frontend requests an eligibility evaluation.
6. The application displays the results.
7. The user submits the booking request.
8. The backend revalidates the request.
9. The database checks scheduling conflicts.
10. The request is stored with the appropriate status.
11. If approval is required, an authorized reviewer receives the request.
12. The reviewer approves or rejects it.
13. The user receives an in-app notification.
14. The user checks in when permitted.
15. The user completes the resource handover.
16. The system records the return condition.
17. The booking is completed.

